  "mechanismSummary": "Butyllithium reacts as the butyl anion, a very strong base: its carbon lone pair takes a proton from the carbon next to P⁺, and the C–H bonding pair stays on that carbon. The ylide has a carbanion next to the phosphonium ion, ready to attack a carbonyl group (the Wittig reaction).",
